    "summary": "Example Hazelbox allows unauthenticated remote code execution through plugin manifest deserialization",
    "description": "## Summary\n\nHazelbox 2.4.0 introduced plugin manifests that the server loads with an unrestricted deserializer. Any HTTP caller can upload a manifest, and loading it runs code chosen by the caller.\n\n## Details\n\nThe upload endpoint does not require a session when the server runs with its default settings, and the manifest loader accepts arbitrary object types.\n\n## Impact\n\nAn attacker who can reach the affected endpoint can exploit this without prior access.\n\n## Patches\n\nFixed in 2.6.1, which loads manifests as plain data and requires a session for uploads.",
    "type": "reviewed",
    "severity": "critical",
    "repository_advisory_url": null,
    "source_code_location": "https://example.com/src/example-hazelbox",
